@anon.8028f6bc2b2948ad00199b8e9b8fe7f2.465 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [605 x i8] }> <{ [605 x i8] c"The direction along which the items are stacked. Possible values are:\0A\0A- `{ltr}`: Left to right.\0A- `{rtl}`: Right to left.\0A- `{ttb}`: Top to bottom.\0A- `{btt}`: Bottom to top.\0A\0AYou can use the `start` and `end` methods to obtain the initial and\0Afinal points (respectively) of a direction, as `alignment`. You can also\0Ause the `axis` method to determine whether a direction is\0A`{\22horizontal\22}` or `{\22vertical\22}`. The `inv` method returns a\0Adirection's inverse direction.\0A\0AFor example, `{ttb.start()}` is `top`, `{ttb.end()}` is `bottom`,\0A`{ttb.axis()}` is `{\22vertical\22}` and `{ttb.inv()}` is equal to `btt`." }>, align 1
